      "problem": "Find the greatest common divisor of $506$ and $207.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}506 & = & 207(2) & + & 92 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 207 & = & 92(2) & + & 23 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 92 & = & 23(4) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $23.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $506$ and $207$ is $23.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(506,207)=23.\n$$",
